.Dd October 19, 2026
.Dt PTHREAD_QUERY_NP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pthread_query_all_np ,
.Nm pthread_query_np
.Nd query thread information
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libpthread
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In pthread.h
.In pthread_np.h
.Ft int
.Fo pthread_query_np
.Fa "pthread_t thread"
.Fa "struct pthread_info_np *info"
.Fa "size_t bufsz"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo pthread_query_all_np
.Fa "struct pthread_info_np *info"
.Fa "size_t *bufsz"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn pthread_query_np
function returns the
.Fx
threading library implementation-specific information about
the thread specified by the
.Fa thread
argument.
The
.Fa info
argument must point to a
.Vt struct pthread_info_np
structure, which is filled with the following information
if the corresponding thread is found:
.Bd -literal
struct pthread_info_np {
	size_t pthread_info_size;
	pthread_t thread;
	long lwpid;
	enum pthread_state_np state;
	int flags;
	int cancel_state;
	int *errno_location;
	struct tcb *tcb;
	struct uexterror *exterr;
	char name[128];
};
.Ed
.Pp
The meaning of the structure fields is the following:
.Bl -tag -width pthread_info_size
.It Va pthread_info_size
The size of the structure.
If new fields are added in the future, it is guaranteed they will be
added at the end of the
.Vt pthread_info_np
structure.
.It Va thread
The thread identifier, as defined by the threading library.
.It Va lwpid
The thread identifier, as defined by the kernel.
See
.Xr pthread_getthreadid_np 3 .
.It Va state
The state of the thread.
Can be one of the following values:
.Bl -tag -width PTHREAD_STATE_SUSPENDED_NP
.It Dv PTHREAD_STATE_RUNNING_NP
Thread is runnable.
.It Dv PTHREAD_STATE_SUSPENDED_NP
Thread was suspended, see
.Xr pthread_suspend_np 3 .
.It Dv PTHREAD_STATE_DEAD_NP
Thread has exited but was not yet reclaimed by
.Xr pthread_join 3 .
.El
.It Va flags
Additional information about the reported thread is provided
by the following flags:
.Bl -tag -width PTHREAD_INFO_DETACHED_NP
.It Dv PTHREAD_INFO_DETACHED_NP
Set if the thread is detached, see
.Xr pthread_attr_setdetachstate 3
and
.Xr pthread_detach 3 .
.It Dv PTHREAD_INFO_INITIAL_NP
Set if the thread was the first thread in the process,
that is it was executing the
.Fn main
function in the process.
.El
.It Va cancel_state
Provides information about the thread cancellability state,
as flags.
The following flags are defined:
.Bl -tag -width PTHREAD_INFO_CANCEL_AT_POINT_NP
.It Dv PTHREAD_INFO_CANCEL_ENABLED_NP
Cancellation is enabled, see
.Xr pthread_setcancelstate 3 .
.It Dv PTHREAD_INFO_CANCEL_ASYNC_NP
Thread cancellation is asynchronous, see
.Xr pthread_setcanceltype 3 .
.It Dv PTHREAD_INFO_CANCEL_PENDING_NP
The cancel event is pending, see
.Xr pthread_cancel 3 .
.It Dv PTHREAD_INFO_CANCEL_AT_POINT_NP
The thread is executing at a cancellation point.
.It Dv PTHREAD_INFO_CANCEL_IN_PROG_NP
The cancellation is in progress.
In particular, the stack unwinding might happen.
.El
.It Va errno_location
The address of the thread-private instance of the
.Xr errno 3
variable.
.It Va tcb
The address of the architecture-specific thread control block.
The
.In machine/tls.h
header provides the definition of
.Vt struct tcb .
.It Va exterr
The location of the thread-private instance of the
.Vt struct uexterror ,
used by the kernel to pass extended information about errors
from system calls.
See
.Xr exterror 9 .
.It Va name
Name of the thread, as set by
.Xr pthread_setname_np 3 .
.El
.Pp
The
.Fa bufsz
argument must specify the size of the passed structure.
At most
.Fa bufsz
bytes are copied to it.
The
.Va pthread_info_size
member reports the size of the buffer needed for
the full structure,
if the library has updated its definition.
The system guarantees that the layout of existing members
never changes.
.Pp
The
.Fn pthread_query_all_np
function returns the information about all threads in the calling
process.
The buffer pointed to by the
.Fa info
argument must have the size in bytes as provided by the value
pointed to by the
.Fa bufsz
argument.
To iterate over the buffer, increment the pointer to the previous
.Vt pthread_info_np
structure by its
.Va pthread_info_size
member.
The
.Fa bufsz
location is always updated with the size of the buffer required
to report all threads.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
If successful, the described functions return zero.
Otherwise an error number is returned to indicate the error or
special condition.
.Sh ERRORS
The
.Fn pthread_query_np
and
.Fn pthread_query_all_np
functions will fail if:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EAGAIN
The threading library was not yet initialized.
.El
.Pp
The
.Fn pthread_query_np
function also fails if:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er ESRCH
The passed
.Fa thread
argument does not designate a valid thread.
.El
.Pp
The
.Fn pthread_query_all_np
function also fails if:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er ENOMEM
The value pointed to by the
.Fa bufsz
argument is too small.
The value is updated with the required size of the buffer.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pthread 3 ,
.Xr pthread_create 3 ,
.Xr pthread_np 3
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Fn pthread_query_np
and
.Fn pthread_query_all_np
functions are an
.Fx
extension.
.Sh HISTORY
The described functions first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh CAVEATS
The
.Fn pthread_query_np
and
.Fn pthread_query_all_np
functions expose the internal transient state of the C runtime.
A running thread changes its state over time.
As such, it is up to the consumer of the interface to accommodate the
temporal nature of the reported values.
.Pp
For instance, the
.Va thread
thread library identifier can be reused
after the exited thread is joined, or,
for a detached thread, reclaimed.
The
.Va lwpid
kernel thread identifier can be reused immediately after the
thread exits.
Similarly,
.Va errno_location ,
.Va tcb ,
and
.Va exterr
pointers are only guaranteed to point to valid objects while
the thread has not exited.
